<article class="env-lemma" id="0852">
  <p><a class="environment-identifier" href="/tag/0852">Lemma <span data-tag="0852">70.6.10</span>.</a> Notation and assumptions as in Situation <a href="/tag/084W" data-tag="084W">70.6.1</a>. If </p>
  <p><ol>
  <li><p>
$f$ is an isomorphism, 
</p>
</li><li><p>
$f_0$ is locally of finite presentation, 
</p>
</li>
</ol></p>
  <p> then $f_ i$ is an isomorphism for some $i \geq 0$. </p>
</article><article class="env-proof">
    <p>
      <strong>Proof.</strong>
      Being an isomorphism is equivalent to being étale, universally injective, and surjective, see Morphisms of Spaces, Lemma <a href="/tag/05W5" data-tag="05W5">67.51.2</a>. Thus the lemma follows from Lemmas <a href="/tag/07SL" data-tag="07SL">70.6.2</a>, <a href="/tag/07SN" data-tag="07SN">70.6.4</a>, and <a href="/tag/084X" data-tag="084X">70.6.5</a>. 
      <span class="qed">$\square$</span>
    </p>
</article>